module Core

### The clock: the date and time (`Clock.now()`) and a clock that only goes forward (`Clock.monotonic()`) for
### measuring time and for deadlines. Every value is the same clock, so the routines are called on the type.
### :see: {Moment}, {Duration}, {CpuClock}
record Clock
    pass

### The processor time the process has used (`CpuClock.now()`), all its threads together. Every value is the same
### clock, so the routines are called on the type.
### :see: {Clock}, {Duration}
record CpuClock
    pass

### Reads the date and time.
### :returns: The current moment (UTC).
common routine Clock.now() -> Moment
    return C::rf_moment_now()

### Reads a clock that only goes forward: the time since a start the operating system chooses. For measuring time and
### for deadlines (`Clock.monotonic() + 30ms`), not for the date. Changing the system's date doesn't move it.
### :returns: The reading. Subtract two readings to get the time between them.
common routine Clock.monotonic() -> Duration
    return C::rf_clock_monotonic()

### Reads the processor time the process has used, all its threads together.
### :returns: The reading. Subtract two readings to get the processor time between them.
common routine CpuClock.now() -> Duration
    return C::rf_cpu_clock_now()
